## 2026-09-05 — Spec 009 Managed Firefox Launch Validated End to End

- Closed the handoff's top loose end: `zuzz-media.service` had never been started since the snap-profile fix (`-P zuzz-media`) landed, so only the direct launch was proven. Stopped the stray unmanaged Firefox (pid 11642) left running from the profile test and started the service.
- The managed path works. `zuzz-media.service` reports active/running with main PID 16535 executing `/snap/firefox/8763/usr/lib/firefox/firefox --no-remote -P zuzz-media --kiosk https://zuzz.tv` inside the unit cgroup, with the expected Firefox content/tab/rdd/utility children indicating the site rendered. No AppArmor profile-lock denials and no re-creation of the existing profile.
- Confirmed the deployed launcher at `~/.local/bin/launch-zuzz` is byte-identical to `scripts/launch-zuzz.sh`, so the validated behavior is the behavior in version control.
- **New defect observed: `media-home.service` now ends in `failed` state when the launcher stops it.** Kodi's main process exited on SIGTERM (status 143) at 00:14:07, but the `kodi.bin` child (pid 10707) survived to the unit's `final-sigterm` timeout and was SIGKILLed at 00:14:17, leaving `Result: exit-code`. Firefox still launched correctly, because the launcher does not gate on the stop's exit status. This is the same Kodi bounded-stop fragility recorded earlier in this spec and in Spec 007, now reproducing as a hard unit failure rather than a slow stop.
- The failure is recoverable: `launch-zuzz --restore` runs `systemctl --user start media-home.service`, which resets the failed state. It is not being fixed here — it is direct evidence for the Spec 015 decision to retire the Kodi-launch half of `media-home.service`, which removes this orchestration entirely rather than hardening it.
- Validation run before commit: `bash -n` on all 13 repository scripts; `systemd-analyze --user verify config/systemd/user/zuzz-media.service` clean (the unrelated pre-existing `spice-vdagent` warning filtered); `desktop-file-validate config/applications/zuzz.desktop` clean; `git diff --check` clean; and a scan of every new/changed file for private-key headers, likely secret assignments, and MAC addresses, with no matches. ShellCheck remains unavailable.
- Monthly security check: the stack is Bash, systemd units, desktop entries, and Markdown with no application package manager, so no dependency-vulnerability scan applies. Secret and key scans were performed this session and on 2026-09-04, satisfying the 30-day requirement.
- Spec 009 T011 owner acceptance remains open: projector presentation, on-screen-keyboard typing in a website field, streaming login/playback, close/relaunch account persistence, and Kodi restoration on stop all still need couch confirmation. T004-T006 remain open for the same reason.

